    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d318-a3">

                <pb facs="0336" n="330" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg330"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">General Reyes to Mr.
                            Braida.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Juan del Norte</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-08-22"><hi rendition="#italic">August 22,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your very attentive
                    communication of this date, together with the exposition, a copy of which you
                    inclose the same, which has been brought to your knowledge by two American
                    citizens. I am very sorry not to be able to accede to your desire, for it is my
                    duty to comply strictly with the written instructions placed in my hands by
                    Minister José Madriz, the representative of the executive power on the Atlantic
                    Coast. He has not consigned in these instructions the faculty and power to give
                    them, the political prisoners, liberty to leave the country, who came guarded by
                    the forces which I command.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. Reyes.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
